      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y &=2 \\\\ -6x-11y &=-8 \\\\ 4x+6y &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -11 & -8 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -11 & -8 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(3){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, select: The system is consistent independent.",
